 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs and internal 2.5 V reference (REFOUT never driven): every conversion returns the 0 V differential code 000h",
  "only HOLDA starts a conversion (the schema has one convst pin); HOLDB and HOLDC, the A-B-C conversion queue and the ignoring of further HOLD pulses until the conversion is done are not modeled",
  "the six output registers: a read at address A2 A1 A0 = 000..101 returns DB15 = 1 (data valid), DB14..DB12 = that channel's Table 2 code and the 0 V result; the data-valid flag is always 1 (after reset/power-up the cleared registers would read DB15 = 0)",
  "cycle mode (110: A0, A1, B0, B1, C0, C1 on successive reads) and FIFO mode (111: three registers per channel, oldest first) always return channel A0's word",
  "BYTE = 1 (8-bit bus: low byte on DB7..DB0 at the first RD, high byte at the second) is not modeled",
  "the conversion is clocked by the external CLOCK (12.5 clocks to the output latch, 16 clocks per conversion); the model uses the 1.75 us conversion time at fCLK = 8 MHz; bus float delay is not specified (tDf 0)",
  "pin names: the minus sign of CH xx- is written '-'"
